WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.740
- People need people who listen.

00:00:03.740 --> 00:00:06.809
- People need people and then

00:00:06.809 --> 00:00:08.937
people need people that 
listen and then people

00:00:08.937 --> 00:00:13.585
need people that 
listen and do something.

00:00:13.585 --> 00:00:17.028
("Lazy Lover" by Common Souls)

00:00:51.162 --> 00:00:52.418
- [Claude] When 
I was a kid I wanted to

00:00:52.418 --> 00:00:55.618
be a philanthropist 
and a movie director

00:00:55.618 --> 00:00:58.301
but what I realized was that I
wanted to help people back then.

00:00:58.301 --> 00:01:01.190
Way back in those days.

00:01:07.616 --> 00:01:11.640
My job is to have 
relationships with the people

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:14.522
that I work with 
and that I work for.

00:01:14.522 --> 00:01:18.557
The difference between 
values and strengths

00:01:18.557 --> 00:01:23.550
as well as the difference 
between strengths and skills.

00:01:24.510 --> 00:01:27.520
And so I work for 700+ people,

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:30.430
I work with 700+ people.

00:01:30.430 --> 00:01:35.104
I have a wonderful team 
that also services 700+ people.

00:01:35.104 --> 00:01:37.284
Any other relationships, 
there's a ton

00:01:37.284 --> 00:01:40.232
but I'd love to just hear 
some of them between skill,

00:01:40.232 --> 00:01:42.278
strength, values.

00:01:42.278 --> 00:01:43.854
- [Sam] I put home 
for values because

00:01:43.854 --> 00:01:47.809
I think that, you 
talk about this a lot,

00:01:47.809 --> 00:01:49.846
that you want everyone to 
feel when they come to work

00:01:49.846 --> 00:01:51.945
to feel like they're in a place
that's comfortable for them,

00:01:51.945 --> 00:01:53.490
safe space.

00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:56.843
Home I feel like is a word that
means a lot of these things.

00:01:56.843 --> 00:01:58.637
It means empathy, 
it means inclusion,

00:01:58.637 --> 00:01:59.604
it means trust,

00:01:59.604 --> 00:02:01.514
you go home and 
that's where you're safe.

00:02:01.514 --> 00:02:02.431
- Yep.

00:02:02.431 --> 00:02:04.279
- [Sam] I feel like we 
have a responsibility to create

00:02:04.279 --> 00:02:06.526
a home here if we can.
- Yeah.

00:02:06.526 --> 00:02:10.796
I, 1000% agree.

00:02:10.796 --> 00:02:14.804
DRock was asking me today 
what my morning routine is

00:02:14.804 --> 00:02:16.099
and so I was 
telling him about it

00:02:16.099 --> 00:02:17.385
which is probably 
boring to you guys

00:02:17.385 --> 00:02:18.932
so I won't tell you about it.
(group laughter)

00:02:18.932 --> 00:02:21.735
But a lot of the 
times I prep myself,

00:02:21.735 --> 00:02:24.214
I might, if I'm talking to 
my best friend on the phone

00:02:24.214 --> 00:02:25.401
or if I'm listening to music,

00:02:25.401 --> 00:02:29.091
I'm prepping 
myself to literally

00:02:29.091 --> 00:02:32.160
make space so that we can

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:35.075
make people feel safe

00:02:35.075 --> 00:02:37.299
physically and 
psychologically safe

00:02:37.299 --> 00:02:39.976
every single day to 
be their best selves.

00:02:39.976 --> 00:02:42.563
That's it. That is 
my number one mission.

00:02:42.563 --> 00:02:44.032
That's what Sam 
was talking about

00:02:44.032 --> 00:02:46.585
in terms of making 
people feel at home

00:02:46.585 --> 00:02:50.308
or creating a home 
for 600, 700 people.

00:02:50.308 --> 00:02:52.663
But what that means to me is

00:02:52.663 --> 00:02:56.073
to have belief in 700+ people

00:02:56.073 --> 00:02:57.753
no matter what happens.

00:02:57.753 --> 00:03:00.923
I think the belief in 
people and understanding that

00:03:00.923 --> 00:03:02.616
people are 
choosing to be at Vayner

00:03:02.616 --> 00:03:04.885
for a very specific reason.

00:03:04.885 --> 00:03:07.154
They could go to any 
of the other agencies,

00:03:07.154 --> 00:03:08.555
which are wonderful,

00:03:08.555 --> 00:03:11.024
but people choose to come here,

00:03:11.024 --> 00:03:13.393
I truly believe, 
because of the culture

00:03:13.393 --> 00:03:16.963
and because of the exceptional 
work that we've been doing.

00:03:16.963 --> 00:03:20.300
The past 20 years that 
I've spent in agency life

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:22.668
has taught me how to be agile.

00:03:22.668 --> 00:03:25.695
Taught me how to 
embrace change and risk

00:03:25.695 --> 00:03:27.374
and it's taught me 
how to seek knowledge

00:03:27.374 --> 00:03:30.210
from all people and arenas.

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:32.979
It's taught me how to read a
room and stay ahead of the curve

00:03:32.979 --> 00:03:35.182
and on the right 
side of history rather

00:03:35.182 --> 00:03:38.285
than paddling 
against the current.

00:03:38.285 --> 00:03:42.217
So when I say, 
"How do we light people up?"

00:03:42.217 --> 00:03:43.623
This is a big 
question for us because

00:03:43.623 --> 00:03:47.880
we are serving other people 
and we work for the greater.

00:03:47.880 --> 00:03:50.197
This is my question to 
myself every single day

00:03:50.197 --> 00:03:52.899
which is how do I light 
you guys up? You know?

00:03:52.899 --> 00:03:54.768
I have something up 
in my room right now

00:03:54.768 --> 00:03:56.670
which says, 
"How do you light people up?"

00:03:56.670 --> 00:03:58.071
And I keep it 
there for a reason.

00:03:58.071 --> 00:04:00.307
I keep it there to see 
how many people look at that

00:04:00.307 --> 00:04:04.277
white board when they come 
in and does that inspire them.

00:04:04.277 --> 00:04:07.009
So I'd like to think 
I'd light people up all day.

00:04:07.009 --> 00:04:09.983
If I do it half a day, 
I'm lucky, right?

00:04:09.983 --> 00:04:11.685
I believe Gary 
lights people up all day.

00:04:11.685 --> 00:04:13.386
I believe you 
light up people all day.

00:04:13.386 --> 00:04:16.223
I want to know how many people

00:04:16.223 --> 00:04:19.192
look at that 
white board and think,

00:04:19.192 --> 00:04:21.628
"How can I light 
someone else's day up?"

00:04:21.628 --> 00:04:24.935
How can I light them up?
It's not all about me.

00:04:24.935 --> 00:04:28.838
How can I light 
someone else's day up?

00:04:28.838 --> 00:04:29.970
That's what we do.

00:04:29.970 --> 00:04:31.938
I know what my 
purpose is every single day

00:04:31.938 --> 00:04:35.041
when I come in to work and I
know what my purpose is in life

00:04:35.041 --> 00:04:37.577
so I can use all of 
that passion to say,

00:04:37.577 --> 00:04:40.813
"Hey Justin, come on, what do
you want to do? Let's do this."

00:04:40.813 --> 00:04:41.815
Know what I mean?

00:04:41.815 --> 00:04:43.216
Jo Beth, what 
do you want to own?

00:04:43.216 --> 00:04:45.785
- [Jo Beth] I think 
the fact that she trusts me

00:04:45.785 --> 00:04:49.422
and the team to do what 
she knows that we'll do

00:04:49.422 --> 00:04:52.255
the best job ever at

00:04:52.255 --> 00:04:55.095
is inspiring for me

00:04:55.095 --> 00:04:56.730
to go out and kill it every day.

00:04:56.730 --> 00:04:59.065
- We are family 
and beyond a family,

00:04:59.065 --> 00:05:00.700
we are friends.

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:04.305
There's such a camaraderie here

00:05:04.305 --> 00:05:08.575
and to come into the door 
and feel it is like nothing else

00:05:08.575 --> 00:05:11.678
every single day.
It's magical.

00:05:11.678 --> 00:05:13.614
- So the hard thing about 
actually working with Claude is

00:05:13.614 --> 00:05:15.749
that she teaches you and 
everybody around you

00:05:15.749 --> 00:05:17.551
something every single day.

00:05:17.551 --> 00:05:19.586
- [Claude] The relationship 
I then get to have with them

00:05:19.586 --> 00:05:21.321
is feeling like 
I got the golden ticket.

00:05:21.321 --> 00:05:24.460
I get to sit with them and

00:05:24.460 --> 00:05:27.460
listen to them and 
watch them grow.

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:30.145
That's like the 
biggest honor in the world.

00:05:30.145 --> 00:05:32.699
- [Gary] So as of today, 
starting on Monday,

00:05:32.699 --> 00:05:37.103
we now have a 
Chief Heart Officer. Alright?

00:05:37.103 --> 00:05:41.141
And that Chief Heart Officer 
is actually here.

00:05:41.141 --> 00:05:45.212
So I think we should 
grab our Chief Heart Officer.

00:05:45.212 --> 00:05:48.029
(audience applause)

00:05:48.029 --> 00:05:52.473
("Bandaids Pt. 2" 
by Common Souls)

00:05:52.473 --> 00:05:53.486
- [Sam] I think my 
favorite Claude moment

00:05:53.486 --> 00:05:56.923
was when she was 
introduced as CHO

00:05:56.923 --> 00:05:58.925
'cause she had 
been here previously,

00:05:58.925 --> 00:06:03.336
obviously as an 
SVP and when

00:06:03.336 --> 00:06:06.533
Gary introduced 
the name of the role,

00:06:06.533 --> 00:06:08.868
everyone kinda started 
to like buzz a little bit

00:06:08.868 --> 00:06:10.971
and then as she 
rounded the corner

00:06:10.971 --> 00:06:12.472
and just kind of 
raised her hands in the air,

00:06:12.472 --> 00:06:13.673
we were all cheering for her.

00:06:13.673 --> 00:06:15.675
Just that moment 
knowing she was back

00:06:15.675 --> 00:06:17.544
and knowing the 
capacity that she was back in

00:06:17.544 --> 00:06:19.813
was just, it was 
just really cool.

00:06:19.813 --> 00:06:21.248
We were all just so happy.

00:06:21.248 --> 00:06:24.684
People that hadn't met 
her before were confused

00:06:24.684 --> 00:06:26.786
but knew that it 
was a special moment

00:06:26.786 --> 00:06:29.589
so definitely the 
favorite moment for Claude.

00:06:29.589 --> 00:06:32.592
- I was on HR for 
a little over a year

00:06:32.592 --> 00:06:35.195
when Claude joined the team.

00:06:35.195 --> 00:06:40.533
And it was the best day 
ever when she did. (laughs)

00:06:40.533 --> 00:06:43.270
- [Claude] So all my experiences
I think throughout the years

00:06:43.270 --> 00:06:45.405
and throughout studying 
and psychology and spirituality

00:06:45.405 --> 00:06:48.742
and all these things kind 
of started to create this soup,

00:06:48.742 --> 00:06:51.544
kind of this minestrone soup of

00:06:51.544 --> 00:06:54.114
being passionate about people.

00:06:54.114 --> 00:06:55.682
Wanting to unlock people.

00:06:55.682 --> 00:06:57.684
Wanting to facilitate 
growth and change with people

00:06:57.684 --> 00:06:59.853
and yet I was a strategist.

00:06:59.853 --> 00:07:01.688
I was understanding 
human behavior

00:07:01.688 --> 00:07:04.090
and how I could 
sell more toothpaste.

00:07:04.090 --> 00:07:06.760
I knew how I could 
sell more toilet paper.

00:07:06.760 --> 00:07:09.396
I understood how I could 
bring peace of mind

00:07:09.396 --> 00:07:13.519
to a mom in Italy 
with spaghetti sauce.

00:07:13.519 --> 00:07:17.595
But I needed more and more 
experiences working with people

00:07:17.595 --> 00:07:20.675
to understand how we all

00:07:20.675 --> 00:07:22.815
dive in the pool together.

00:07:22.815 --> 00:07:24.500
Who swims this way, 
who swims that way,

00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:26.246
who's drowning, 
all of that stuff.

00:07:26.246 --> 00:07:31.032
So, that's a long-winded 
way of saying that

00:07:31.032 --> 00:07:33.167
it took me a short 
lifetime to get here.

00:07:33.167 --> 00:07:35.422
- [Justin] Claude's such a 
hybrid of understanding

00:07:35.422 --> 00:07:40.427
the business needs because she's
already a king of that trade,

00:07:40.427 --> 00:07:42.095
a master of that trade,

00:07:42.095 --> 00:07:46.533
but she's also a master of 
reading people like Gary is.

00:07:46.533 --> 00:07:49.836
Those two, along with several 
other people in this agency,

00:07:49.836 --> 00:07:52.339
can walk into a room, 
read what's going on

00:07:52.339 --> 00:07:57.143
and understand what to do next
in the middle of a conversation.

00:07:57.143 --> 00:07:58.445
- [Claude] When I left Vayner,

00:07:58.445 --> 00:08:00.880
the reason I left was 
because all I wanted to do,

00:08:00.880 --> 00:08:04.665
all I wanted to do 
was be with people.

00:08:04.665 --> 00:08:06.886
Build relationships, coach,

00:08:06.886 --> 00:08:08.288
I thought that 
maybe I would start

00:08:08.288 --> 00:08:10.690
my own coaching 
practice at 47 years old.

00:08:10.690 --> 00:08:13.760
I thought maybe I would 
go back to school and

00:08:13.760 --> 00:08:17.468
get my master's in social work.

00:08:17.468 --> 00:08:20.900
I didn't know that I'd end 
up as a Chief Heart Officer.

00:08:20.900 --> 00:08:23.636
I love it. It makes 
so much sense.

00:08:23.636 --> 00:08:26.327
So much sense.

00:08:26.327 --> 00:08:27.874
But throughout all those years,

00:08:27.874 --> 00:08:29.676
I learned what listening does,

00:08:29.676 --> 00:08:30.877
I learned what empathy does,

00:08:30.877 --> 00:08:34.047
I learned that you absolutely 
need to take up space.

00:08:34.047 --> 00:08:35.548
You deserve to take up space.

00:08:35.548 --> 00:08:37.323
If you've been invited 
to that meeting,

00:08:37.323 --> 00:08:39.947
you're there for a
reason, so speak.

00:08:42.688 --> 00:08:46.393
I believe in people and I see 
the good in the every day.

00:08:46.393 --> 00:08:49.763
I build teams rooted 
in a generosity of spirit

00:08:49.763 --> 00:08:52.132
and a belief in possibility.

00:08:52.132 --> 00:08:55.702
I unlock people so that they 
can become their own champions

00:08:55.702 --> 00:09:00.340
and I celebrate the little 
as well as the big victories.

00:09:00.340 --> 00:09:02.675
I believe that there's 
magic in every moment

00:09:02.675 --> 00:09:06.046
and that people need 
to be allowed to dream.

00:09:06.046 --> 00:09:09.315
Truly I believe in that 
glimmer in a teammate's eyes

00:09:09.315 --> 00:09:11.785
and I know how to 
push that glimmer until

00:09:11.785 --> 00:09:13.787
it becomes a full-blown smile.

00:09:15.855 --> 00:09:17.424
But there's a give and take, 
there's a dance and

00:09:17.424 --> 00:09:18.858
I think in all of these years

00:09:18.858 --> 00:09:21.494
I've learned what 
that dance is about and

00:09:21.494 --> 00:09:23.580
now I'm at a place 
where I get to work

00:09:23.580 --> 00:09:26.166
with 700 people-plus 
every single day.

00:09:26.166 --> 00:09:30.070
I get to work like that with Gary 
and I get to work and grow

00:09:30.070 --> 00:09:33.390
and foster an amazing 
team that's just hungry.

00:09:33.390 --> 00:09:36.309
They're just sponges.

00:09:36.309 --> 00:09:39.379
So it took a long 
time but I'm here and

00:09:39.379 --> 00:09:40.780
I wouldn't be any other place.

00:09:40.780 --> 00:09:44.117
- It's also so awesome to 
have a CEO and to have a boss

00:09:44.117 --> 00:09:47.921
who truly cares about 
the people within the walls.

00:09:47.921 --> 00:09:49.289
And I think that's 
what makes coming to work

00:09:49.289 --> 00:09:51.311
so worth it and so awesome.

00:09:51.311 --> 00:09:54.527
- You know, Claude is 
one of the few individuals

00:09:54.527 --> 00:09:57.864
that I've ever met in my life that 
makes me feel the way I feel

00:09:57.864 --> 00:10:01.607
and so to create this position

00:10:01.607 --> 00:10:03.837
which is more than Mark,

00:10:03.837 --> 00:10:07.507
more than AJ, 
more than James, more than Scott,

00:10:07.507 --> 00:10:09.695
more than Segal or Mickey,

00:10:09.695 --> 00:10:14.372
to create a position 
that really is me, right?

00:10:14.372 --> 00:10:16.749
The scalable version 
of what I do with you guys

00:10:16.749 --> 00:10:19.486
one-on-one in those meetings 
and have the autonomy

00:10:19.486 --> 00:10:22.222
to make decisions 
that make no sense on paper

00:10:22.222 --> 00:10:24.858
but make a whole 
lot of sense on heart.

00:10:24.858 --> 00:10:28.294
I want to build 
the best, greatest,

00:10:28.294 --> 00:10:29.809
let me rephrase,

00:10:29.809 --> 00:10:32.853
we (audience laughter)

00:10:32.853 --> 00:10:37.897
we want to build the single 
greatest human organization

00:10:37.897 --> 00:10:39.439
in the history of times.

00:10:39.439 --> 00:10:41.241
- [Claude] So when I think 
people are meeting with me

00:10:41.241 --> 00:10:42.442
it's not to get Gary.

00:10:42.442 --> 00:10:43.710
They can get Gary.

00:10:43.710 --> 00:10:47.113
His door in completely 
open and he's available.

00:10:47.113 --> 00:10:50.350
I think they're looking for

00:10:50.350 --> 00:10:51.284
why am I here.

00:10:51.284 --> 00:10:53.953
I think a lot of times 
people ask me what I do here.

00:10:53.953 --> 00:10:55.522
How did I get here?

00:10:55.522 --> 00:10:59.058
They're interested in 
why an old fogie like me is

00:10:59.058 --> 00:11:00.493
running around with 
a bunch of Millennials.

00:11:00.493 --> 00:11:04.397
I don't know but 
I complement him,

00:11:04.397 --> 00:11:08.536
I believe, 
by coming at situations

00:11:08.536 --> 00:11:09.936
in a slightly different way.

00:11:09.936 --> 00:11:13.206
Some times more emotional, 
some times more heartfelt.

00:11:13.206 --> 00:11:18.099
Some times with a little 
bit more vinegar than honey.

00:11:18.099 --> 00:11:20.013
Some times calling 
them on their bullshit

00:11:20.013 --> 00:11:23.172
in a different 
way than he might.

00:11:23.172 --> 00:11:26.519
And some times I know 
that he's had a conversation

00:11:26.519 --> 00:11:27.754
with them which has been honey

00:11:27.754 --> 00:11:31.090
so I'll come in and look at it
with a slightly different slant

00:11:31.090 --> 00:11:35.755
to help someone or 
assist someone in getting

00:11:35.755 --> 00:11:38.598
A, to the answer or the answer
that we'd like them to get to.

00:11:38.598 --> 00:11:41.568
On another level, I might 
need one answer for him

00:11:41.568 --> 00:11:44.737
or he might need to 
tell me one adjective

00:11:44.737 --> 00:11:48.841
and I know exactly the direction
I need to take a conversation.

00:11:48.841 --> 00:11:50.777
Gary and I speak all the time.

00:11:50.777 --> 00:11:52.925
We're in constant communication.

00:11:52.925 --> 00:11:55.481
And actually, we're 
two sides of the same coin.

00:11:55.481 --> 00:11:58.314
In lockstep when it 
comes to heart and hustle.

00:11:58.314 --> 00:11:59.986
I mean, we're really focused on

00:11:59.986 --> 00:12:03.590
creating the greatest 
Honey Empire of all time.

00:12:03.590 --> 00:12:05.391
What I've learned 
from working with Gary is

00:12:05.391 --> 00:12:09.247
a completely 
different level of patience.

00:12:09.247 --> 00:12:13.262
A completely different 
level of accountability.

00:12:13.262 --> 00:12:16.639
A completely 
different level of humility.

00:12:16.639 --> 00:12:20.111
I've learned to let go of

00:12:20.111 --> 00:12:22.141
the 99% of stuff 
that you don't need

00:12:22.141 --> 00:12:26.070
and really focus on 
that number 1% North Star.

00:12:27.880 --> 00:12:31.517
Together, Gary and I, 
marry the heart and the hustle.

00:12:31.517 --> 00:12:35.188
I create the strategic 
direction for all things people

00:12:35.188 --> 00:12:36.956
alongside Gary who creates

00:12:36.956 --> 00:12:40.259
the strategic vision 
for all things business.

00:12:40.259 --> 00:12:42.632
And together with our team

00:12:42.632 --> 00:12:46.432
we are building the 
greatest Honey Empire.

00:12:46.432 --> 00:12:49.969
Fueled by people operating 
at the top of their game.

00:12:54.340 --> 00:12:56.843
Simply put, I'm in 
the people business.

00:12:56.843 --> 00:12:59.646
I touch anything and everything

00:12:59.646 --> 00:13:01.247
that has to do with the people

00:13:01.247 --> 00:13:04.648
at VaynerMedia 
and their experiences.

